          "sessionID": "ses_41",
          "messageID": "msg_ses_41_02",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "No, private doesn't make it safe — anyone with repo access (teammates, your TA, CI logs, a future public mirror) can read that key, and it's sitting in history forever even if you delete it now. Rotate the key immediately, then remove it from history with `git filter-repo` or `git rm --cached .env`, and add `.env` to `.gitignore` so it doesn't happen again."
        },
