          "messageID": "msg_ses_41_04",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "No — TS types are erased at compile time, there's no runtime check. If the request body actually has `age: \"20\"`, your function happily receives a string and nothing throws; it just silently misbehaves. You need actual runtime validation (zod, or a manual check) at the boundary where untrusted JSON comes in."
        },
